// stdlib/darwin_pbpk/circ28_blood.sio — saturable erythrocyte binding on the circ28 kernel
//
// circ28 is linear: every vascular state is a whole-blood concentration and
// plasma = blood / bp with one constant blood-to-plasma ratio bp. A drug that
// binds a finite number of sites in the erythrocytes has a concentration
// dependent bp. This file is an engine: it carries no literature parameter
// values; Hct, Bmax and Kd are supplied by the caller.
//
// Binding relation (C_p total plasma concentration, Hct haematocrit, Bmax per
// litre of ERYTHROCYTES, Kd in units of C_p):
//
//   C_blood = (1 - Hct) C_p + Hct Bmax C_p / (Kd + C_p)
//
// Inverse. Put a = 1 - Hct and multiply by (Kd + C_p):
//   a C_p (Kd + C_p) + Hct Bmax C_p = C_b (Kd + C_p)
//   a C_p^2 + (a Kd + Hct Bmax - C_b) C_p - C_b Kd = 0.
// The product of the roots is -C_b Kd / a < 0 for C_b > 0, so there is exactly
// one positive root, with b = a Kd + Hct Bmax - C_b and disc = b^2 + 4 a C_b Kd:
//   C_p = (-b + sqrt(disc)) / (2 a)         (b <= 0: no cancellation)
//   C_p = 2 C_b Kd / (b + sqrt(disc))       (b > 0: the same root, rationalised)
// The second form avoids the cancellation of -b + sqrt(disc) when b is large
// and positive (small C_b, or Kd very large, i.e. linear binding).
//
//   bp(C_b) = C_b / C_p(C_b), strictly decreasing in C_b, with
//     C_b -> 0 : bp -> (1 - Hct) + Hct Bmax / Kd
//     C_b -> inf: bp -> (1 - Hct)
//   bp at C_b <= 0 is defined as the first limit.
//
// Stepping. The kernel keeps ONE bp per factorisation. Before each step this
// wrapper sets p.bp from the current blood concentrations and refactors in
// place (circ28_prepare; skipped when bp is bit-identical to the factored one).
//
// Which concentration defines the effective bp. Chosen: the blood-volume
// weighted mean of all 15 blood states, C_w = sum_k V_k x_k / sum_k V_k, that
// is (mass in blood) / (blood volume), and bp_eff = bp(C_w) (the binding
// function of the mean, not the mean of the binding function).
//   - Mass is the conserved quantity of the kernel (sum V x), and C_w is the
//     one summary of the 15 states that follows from it: it is a blood-mass
//     average, it is smooth in time, and it moves toward the plasma-referenced
//     steady state where every blood state is equal.
//   - It is exact when all blood states are equal (steady state with a
//     clearance acting on the venous plasma only) and when binding is linear
//     (bp constant), whichever summary is used.
//   - The venous pool alone (1.19 L of 5.3 L) carries the whole dose during an
//     intravenous input and is ~100 times the other beds in the first
//     circulation times, so bp(C_ven) would be far too low for the body; the
//     arterial pool has the same defect after the lung, and is blind to the
//     liver, which sees a lower concentration than the artery whenever hepatic
//     extraction is high.
//   - A flow- or ps-weighted mean would favour the bed that dominates one term
//     (exchange or hepatic delivery) and misrepresent the others; there is no
//     weight that is right for all of them, so the mass weight, whose meaning
//     is exact, is used and the error is MEASURED (diagnostic below).
// What one global bp cannot represent. Distribution makes the 15 blood
// concentrations differ (venous >> arterial >> peripheral after a bolus; liver
// vascular below arterial under hepatic extraction), so the true bp_i = bp(C_i)
// differ between beds, and bp(C) is convex, so bp(C_w) differs from the mean of
// bp_i. The kernel divides the local blood concentration by the same bp in the
// exchange of every organ, the venous plasma clearance, the renal clearance and
// the hepatic delivery: each of those terms carries the error of its own bed.
// The cell-bound amount is also taken to equilibrate instantly with plasma
// (slow erythrocyte efflux is not modelled).
//
// Schemes (mode). The coupling bp <-> state is a feedback with gain equal to
// the elasticity e = d ln bp / d ln C_b = 1 - 1/eta, eta = d ln C_b / d ln C_p
// in (0,1]. Blood and tissue exchange in minutes (ps/(bp V) ~ 10^3-10^4 /h), so
// within a step the blood concentration follows bp at once, and any scheme
// that fixes bp from START-of-step information iterates x -> bp(x) with slope e:
// it is unstable when |e| > 1 (when most of the blood drug is bound, eta < 1/2).
// MEASURED (test and report): at steady state with C_b = 48, C_p = 20, e = -2.2,
// modes 0, 1 and 2 all settle on a period-2 cycle with nonsense states
// (negative arterial concentration) at dt = 0.1 and 0.02 h. They are kept for
// small-nonlinearity use and order studies; mode 3 is the default.
//   0 "extrapolate": C_mid = max(0, C_n + (C_n - C_{n-1})/2) from the last two
//        evaluations (as in circ28_ddi.sio, applied to the concentration, which
//        is more nearly linear in time than bp); the first step uses C_n.
//        Second order while stable.
//   1 "lag": C_mid = C_n, first order, unstable for |e| > 1.
//   2 "predictor-corrector": a trial step with bp(C_n) gives C_{n+1}^trial; the
//        state is restored and the real step uses bp(mean(C_n, C_{n+1}^trial)).
//        One fixed-point sweep: second order, same stability limit.
//   3 "implicit midpoint" (default): the root of
//          g(bp) = bp( (C_n + C_{n+1}(bp)) / 2 ) - bp = 0,
//        where C_{n+1}(bp) is the blood-mean concentration after a trial step
//        with that bp (state restored after every trial). C_{n+1} increases with
//        bp and bp(C) decreases with C, so g is strictly decreasing, has exactly
//        one root, and it lies in [1 - Hct, bp_low]; it is found by a bracketed
//        secant (bisection fallback) to |g| <= 1e-11 bp. Unconditionally stable
//        in the coupling, second order (trapezoid in C), at the cost of a few
//        trial steps and refactorisations per step (one near steady state).
// Mass balance. Mass is tracked in blood concentrations x, and the conserved
// quantity is sum V_k x_k, with V_k independent of bp. bp enters only the rates
// (exchange, plasma and renal clearance), and circ28_prepare builds the matrix
// and the elimination coefficients k_ren, k_pla of one step from the same bp, so
// in every step the mass removed from the state equals the mass booked to the
// elimination channels exactly (to rounding), however bp differs from step to
// step. In mode 2 the trial step is undone completely (state and tallies).
//
// The caller owns the Circ28Sys (Madaros handle table): create it once with
// circ28_sys_zero() and pass it to every step. Do not change b.dt after the
// first step.

use darwin_pbpk::circ28::*
use math::pure::{sqrt}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- relation

// Whole-blood concentration from total plasma concentration.
pub fn blood28_blood_from_plasma(hct: f64, bmax: f64, kd: f64, cp: f64) -> f64 with Div {
    return (1.0 - hct) * cp + hct * bmax * cp / (kd + cp)
}

// Total plasma concentration from whole-blood concentration (positive root).
pub fn blood28_plasma_from_blood(hct: f64, bmax: f64, kd: f64, cb: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    if !(cb > 0.0) { return 0.0 }
    let a = 1.0 - hct
    let b = a * kd + hct * bmax - cb
    let disc = b * b + 4.0 * a * cb * kd
    let r = sqrt(disc)
    if b > 0.0 { return 2.0 * cb * kd / (b + r) }
    return (r - b) / (2.0 * a)
}

// bp -> (1 - Hct) + Hct Bmax / Kd as C -> 0.
pub fn blood28_bp_low(hct: f64, bmax: f64, kd: f64) -> f64 with Div {
    return (1.0 - hct) + hct * bmax / kd
}

// bp -> (1 - Hct) as C -> infinity.
pub fn blood28_bp_high(hct: f64) -> f64 {
    return 1.0 - hct
}

// Blood-to-plasma ratio at whole-blood concentration cb.
pub fn blood28_bp(hct: f64, bmax: f64, kd: f64, cb: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    if !(cb > 0.0) { return blood28_bp_low(hct, bmax, kd) }
    return cb / blood28_plasma_from_blood(hct, bmax, kd, cb)
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------- diagnostics

// Blood-volume weighted mean of the 15 blood states (ven, art, 13 vascular).
pub fn blood28_mean_conc(s: &Circ28State, p: Circ28Params) -> f64 with Mut, Div {
    var m = 0.0
    var v = 0.0
    var k: i32 = 0
    while k < 15 {
        var idx = k
        if k >= 2 { idx = circ28_iv(k - 1) }
        let w = circ28_state_volume(p, idx)
        m = m + w * (*s).x[idx]
        v = v + w
        k = k + 1
    }
    return m / v
}

// Largest relative discrepancy |bp(C_i) - bp_used| / bp_used over the 15 blood
// states: how wrong the single bp is for the worst bed.
pub fn blood28_bp_discrepancy(
    s: &Circ28State,
    p: Circ28Params,
    hct: f64,
    bmax: f64,
    kd: f64,
    bp_used: f64
) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    var worst = 0.0
    var k: i32 = 0
    while k < 15 {
        var idx = k
        if k >= 2 { idx = circ28_iv(k - 1) }
        let bi = blood28_bp(hct, bmax, kd, (*s).x[idx])
        var d = (bi - bp_used) / bp_used
        if d < 0.0 { d = 0.0 - d }
        if d > worst { worst = d }
        k = k + 1
    }
    return worst
}

// --------------------------------------------------------------- the engine

pub struct Blood28 {
    pub hct: f64,
    pub bmax: f64,
    pub kd: f64,
    pub dt: f64,
    pub mode: i32,             // see the header: 3 is the default
    pub t: f64,
    pub p: Circ28Params,       // p.bp holds the bp the system is factored with
    pub s: Circ28State,
    pub el: Circ28Elim,
    pub s_save: Circ28State,   // scratch for mode 2
    pub el_save: Circ28Elim,
    pub c_prev: f64,           // C_w at the previous step
    pub hist: i32,
    pub prepared: i32,
    pub bp_used: f64,          // bp of the last step
    pub bp_min: f64,           // extremes of bp_used since the start
    pub bp_max: f64,
    pub disc_last: f64,        // diagnostic at the start of the last step
    pub disc_max: f64,
    pub nfact: i32,            // refactorisations
    pub ntrial: i32,           // trial steps of mode 3
}

pub fn blood28_new(p: Circ28Params, hct: f64, bmax: f64, kd: f64, dt: f64) -> Blood28 with Mut, Div {
    return Blood28 {
        hct: hct,
        bmax: bmax,
        kd: kd,
        dt: dt,
        mode: 3,
        t: 0.0,
        p: p,
        s: circ28_state_zero(),
        el: circ28_elim_zero(),
        s_save: circ28_state_zero(),
        el_save: circ28_elim_zero(),
        c_prev: 0.0,
        hist: 0,
        prepared: 0,
        bp_used: blood28_bp_low(hct, bmax, kd),
        bp_min: 1.0e300,
        bp_max: 0.0,
        disc_last: 0.0,
        disc_max: 0.0,
        nfact: 0,
        ntrial: 0,
    }
}

// 0 extrapolate, 1 lag, 2 predictor-corrector, 3 implicit midpoint (default).
pub fn blood28_set_mode(b: &!Blood28, mode: i32) with Mut {
    (*b).mode = mode
}

// Writes state entry k (0..27); resets the extrapolation history.
pub fn blood28_set_x(b: &!Blood28, k: i32, v: f64) with Mut {
    (*b).s.x[k] = v
    (*b).hist = 0
}

pub fn blood28_get_x(b: &Blood28, k: i32) -> f64 { return (*b).s.x[k] }
pub fn blood28_time(b: &Blood28) -> f64 { return (*b).t }
pub fn blood28_bp_current(b: &Blood28) -> f64 { return (*b).bp_used }
pub fn blood28_bp_min(b: &Blood28) -> f64 { return (*b).bp_min }
pub fn blood28_bp_max(b: &Blood28) -> f64 { return (*b).bp_max }
pub fn blood28_disc_last(b: &Blood28) -> f64 { return (*b).disc_last }
pub fn blood28_disc_max(b: &Blood28) -> f64 { return (*b).disc_max }
pub fn blood28_refactorisations(b: &Blood28) -> i32 { return (*b).nfact }
pub fn blood28_trials(b: &Blood28) -> i32 { return (*b).ntrial }

// Effective whole-blood concentration of the current state (C_w).
pub fn blood28_effective_conc(b: &Blood28) -> f64 with Mut, Div {
    return blood28_mean_conc(&(*b).s, (*b).p)
}

// bp the single-bp approximation would use now (mode-independent: bp(C_w)).
pub fn blood28_effective_bp(b: &Blood28) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    return blood28_bp(
        (*b).hct, (*b).bmax, (*b).kd,
        blood28_mean_conc(&(*b).s, (*b).p)
    )
}

// Venous plasma concentration from the venous blood state with ITS OWN bp
// (not the bp of the step, which is a global effective value).
pub fn blood28_plasma_venous(b: &Blood28) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    return blood28_plasma_from_blood((*b).hct, (*b).bmax, (*b).kd, (*b).s.x[0])
}

// Mass eliminated by all channels (mg).
pub fn blood28_eliminated(b: &Blood28) -> f64 {
    return (*b).el.hepatic + (*b).el.formed + (*b).el.renal + (*b).el.plasma + (*b).el.gut
}

// Mass still in the body (mg).
pub fn blood28_remaining(b: &Blood28) -> f64 with Mut {
    return circ28_total_mass(&(*b).s, (*b).p)
}

// Area under the venous blood curve (mg.h/L).
pub fn blood28_auc_blood(b: &Blood28) -> f64 { return (*b).el.auc_ven }

// Sets p.bp = bp and refactors in place unless it is bit-identical.
fn blood28_set_bp(b: &!Blood28, bp: f64, sys: &!Circ28Sys) with Mut, Div {
    if (*b).prepared == 1 {
        if bp == (*b).p.bp { return }
    }
    (*b).p.bp = bp
    circ28_prepare((*b).p, (*b).dt, sys)
    (*b).prepared = 1
    (*b).nfact = (*b).nfact + 1
}

fn blood28_save(b: &!Blood28) with Mut {
    var k: i32 = 0
    while k < 28 {
        (*b).s_save.x[k] = (*b).s.x[k]
        k = k + 1
    }
    (*b).el_save.hepatic = (*b).el.hepatic
    (*b).el_save.formed = (*b).el.formed
    (*b).el_save.renal = (*b).el.renal
    (*b).el_save.plasma = (*b).el.plasma
    (*b).el_save.gut = (*b).el.gut
    (*b).el_save.auc_ven = (*b).el.auc_ven
    (*b).el_save.auc_art = (*b).el.auc_art
}

fn blood28_restore(b: &!Blood28) with Mut {
    var k: i32 = 0
    while k < 28 {
        (*b).s.x[k] = (*b).s_save.x[k]
        k = k + 1
    }
    (*b).el.hepatic = (*b).el_save.hepatic
    (*b).el.formed = (*b).el_save.formed
    (*b).el.renal = (*b).el_save.renal
    (*b).el.plasma = (*b).el_save.plasma
    (*b).el.gut = (*b).el_save.gut
    (*b).el.auc_ven = (*b).el_save.auc_ven
    (*b).el.auc_art = (*b).el_save.auc_art
}

// g(bp) of mode 3 for a trial step from the saved state; leaves the state
// restored. cn is C_w at the start of the step.
fn blood28_trial(b: &!Blood28, sys: &!Circ28Sys, cn: f64, bp: f64, iv_rate: f64, oral_rate: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    blood28_set_bp(b, bp, sys)
    circ28_step(&!(*b).s, (*b).p, sys, iv_rate, oral_rate, &!(*b).el)
    let c1 = blood28_mean_conc(&(*b).s, (*b).p)
    blood28_restore(b)
    (*b).ntrial = (*b).ntrial + 1
    return blood28_bp((*b).hct, (*b).bmax, (*b).kd, 0.5 * (cn + c1)) - bp
}

// Root of g (mode 3). Expects the state saved with blood28_save.
fn blood28_solve_bp(b: &!Blood28, sys: &!Circ28Sys, cn: f64, iv_rate: f64, oral_rate: f64) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic {
    var lo = blood28_bp_high((*b).hct)
    var hi = blood28_bp_low((*b).hct, (*b).bmax, (*b).kd)
    var x = blood28_bp((*b).hct, (*b).bmax, (*b).kd, cn)
    var gx = blood28_trial(b, sys, cn, x, iv_rate, oral_rate)
    var xp = x
    var gp = gx
    var it: i32 = 0
    while it < 80 {
        var ag = gx
        if ag < 0.0 { ag = 0.0 - ag }
        if ag <= 1.0e-11 * x { return x }
        if gx > 0.0 { lo = x } else { hi = x }
        var xn = x + 0.5 * gx
        if it > 0 {
            let den = gx - gp
            if den != 0.0 { xn = x - gx * (x - xp) / den }
        }
        if !(xn > lo) { xn = 0.5 * (lo + hi) }
        if !(xn < hi) { xn = 0.5 * (lo + hi) }
        xp = x
        gp = gx
        x = xn
        gx = blood28_trial(b, sys, cn, x, iv_rate, oral_rate)
        it = it + 1
    }
    return x
}

// Advances by b.dt. iv_rate (mg/h) enters the venous pool and oral_rate (mg/h)
// gut tissue, both constant over the step.
pub fn blood28_step(b: &!Blood28, sys: &!Circ28Sys, iv_rate: f64, oral_rate: f64) with Mut, Div, Panic {
    let cn = blood28_mean_conc(&(*b).s, (*b).p)
    let hct = (*b).hct
    let bmax = (*b).bmax
    let kd = (*b).kd
    var c_use = cn
    if (*b).mode == 0 {
        if (*b).hist == 1 {
            c_use = cn + 0.5 * (cn - (*b).c_prev)
            if c_use < 0.0 { c_use = 0.0 }
        }
    }
    if (*b).mode == 2 {
        // trial step with bp(C_n), then undo it
        blood28_save(b)
        blood28_set_bp(b, blood28_bp(hct, bmax, kd, cn), sys)
        circ28_step(&!(*b).s, (*b).p, sys, iv_rate, oral_rate, &!(*b).el)
        let c1 = blood28_mean_conc(&(*b).s, (*b).p)
        blood28_restore(b)
        c_use = 0.5 * (cn + c1)
    }
    var bp = blood28_bp(hct, bmax, kd, c_use)
    if (*b).mode == 3 {
        blood28_save(b)
        bp = blood28_solve_bp(b, sys, cn, iv_rate, oral_rate)
    }
    // diagnostic at the start of the step, against the bp actually used
    let dsc = blood28_bp_discrepancy(&(*b).s, (*b).p, hct, bmax, kd, bp)
    (*b).disc_last = dsc
    if dsc > (*b).disc_max { (*b).disc_max = dsc }
    blood28_set_bp(b, bp, sys)
    circ28_step(&!(*b).s, (*b).p, sys, iv_rate, oral_rate, &!(*b).el)
    (*b).bp_used = bp
    if bp < (*b).bp_min { (*b).bp_min = bp }
    if bp > (*b).bp_max { (*b).bp_max = bp }
    (*b).c_prev = cn
    (*b).hist = 1
    (*b).t = (*b).t + (*b).dt
}
